\section{Task duration in the pre-test}
\label{app:task-duration}
\renewcommand{\thefigure}{A\arabic{figure}}
\setcounter{figure}{0}

\begin{figure}[!htbp]
\centering
<<figure-pretest-task-duration, fig.width=6.7, fig.height=4.5>>=
@
\caption{Mean choice-task duration by condition among completed pre-test participants}
\label{fig:task-duration-completes}
\par\smallskip
\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\footnotesize
\textit{Notes.} The pre-test comprises \Sexpr{pretest$n_respondents} eligible
participants who reached the final study screen, submitted all \Sexpr{pretest$n_main_tasks} analytical
tasks, and recorded at least \Sexpr{pretest$minimum_valid_main_choices} valid candidate choices.
The unconstrained, exploratory timed, and arithmetic-cost conditions include
\Sexpr{pretest$baseline$n_respondents}, \Sexpr{pretest$time$n_respondents}, and
\Sexpr{pretest$cost$n_respondents} participants, respectively. Each contributes
one observation to each of the \Sexpr{pretest$n_main_tasks} analytical choice tasks, for
\Sexpr{pretest$n_tasks} task observations. The \Sexpr{pretest$n_practice_tasks} practice tasks
are excluded.
Points report arithmetic means, and bars show pointwise \Sexpr{ci_percent}\% Student-$t$
confidence intervals across respondents within each condition and task.
Time runs from the display of both loaded photographs until manual or automatic
task submission. It includes information acquisition and arithmetic operations
when applicable, but excludes image loading and follow-up questions.
Up to \Sexpr{pretest$allowed_missing_choices} timed submissions without a candidate selection are permitted per
retained interview and remain in the figure. No long durations are removed or
capped. The dotted line marks the exploratory \Sexpr{pretest$deadline_seconds}-second deadline.
Comparisons are descriptive and conditional on study completion, which may
itself be affected by treatment.
\end{minipage}
\end{figure}

