\section{Information acquisition by respondent and candidate gender}
\label{app:respondent-scrutiny}
\renewcommand{\thefigure}{C\arabic{figure}}
\setcounter{figure}{0}

\begin{figure}[!htbp]
\centering
<<figure-respondent-scrutiny, fig.width=7.2, fig.height=4.4, eval=has_model_data>>=
@
\caption{Candidate information acquisition among male and female respondents}
\label{fig:respondent-scrutiny}
\par\smallskip
\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\footnotesize
\textit{Notes.} Panels distinguish male and female respondents. Within each panel,
points show the probability that information about a male or female candidate was
opened at least once in each experimental condition. The points equal the observed
opening rates, not differences between respondent groups. Bars show pointwise
\Sexpr{ci_percent}\% confidence intervals from a saturated binomial-logit model
of condition, candidate gender, respondent gender, and their interactions.
The covariance is clustered by respondent and candidate, with a
positive-semidefinite correction when required. Student-$t$ critical values use
\Sexpr{if (has_model_data) scrutiny_df else 0L} degrees of freedom. Intervals are calculated on the log-odds
scale and transformed to probabilities.
The figure uses \Sexpr{paper_counts$scrutiny_appearances} candidate appearances
from \Sexpr{paper_counts$scrutiny_respondents} eligible completed interviews.
Respondent counts by condition are \Sexpr{if (has_model_data) scrutiny_sample_note else ""}.
Participants reporting another gender identity or not reporting gender are
outside this specific comparison, but remain in the other analyses if eligible.
This excludes \Sexpr{paper_counts$scrutiny_excluded_respondents} completed
respondents from the present figure.
Retained tasks without a candidate selection still contribute their recorded
information-opening outcomes. The measure does not establish that the text was
read or count repeated clicks. These exploratory, completion-conditioned
associations are not causal effects of respondent or candidate gender.
\end{minipage}
\end{figure}

